  "type": "FeatureCollection",
  "description": "The Rock Carvings in Tanum is a collection of petroglyphs located near Tanumshede, Bohusl\u00e4n, Sweden. This heritage landscape is composed of at least 600 rock-cut panels covering an area of some 51 ha (126 acres). Many of the figural motifs are maritime in nature and pertain to the European Bronze Age.",
